WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.610
At certain points in their careers, actors
no longer need to audition for the roles they

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.789
take. Eventually, if they're good enough,
studios offer them roles, and they can pick

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:18.570
and choose as they please. However, the inverse
of that happens too. Sometimes actors are

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:24.789
forced to take roles they don't want at all.
Here are some of the worst.

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:26.710
Channing Tatum

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.949
As the star of Magic Mike and 21 Jump Street,
Channing Tatum is probably one of the biggest

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:37.010
names in Hollywood today. So it may come as
a surprise that he hated acting in one of

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:42.800
the movies that helped him become so well
known: G. I. Joe: The Rise of Cobra. In an

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.690
interview with Howard Stern, Tatum admitted
that he was pushed into doing that movie.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:52.139
Tatum went on to say that, although he was
a fan of the cartoon growing up, the script

00:00:52.139 --> 00:00:58.280
was not good. He also really actually wanted
to play Snake Eyes instead of the lead character.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.389
But he does admit that he felt blessed for
getting the work, even if it didn’t open

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:04.930
up the doors he would have liked.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:05.460
Ed Norton

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:12.659
Primal Fear was only the first film in a three-picture
deal that Ed Norton made with Paramount Studios.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:17.539
It initially wasn’t a bad deal, because
the film got him his start, and an Oscar nomination

00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:23.119
too. Soon after being noticed, numerous studios
offered Norton parts in their films, and he

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:28.219
never got around to making another movie for
Paramount. Finally, Paramount took action,

00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:32.679
and in order for Norton to appear in Fight
Club, he had to negotiate a new deal with

00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:37.929
the studio. Another three years passed, and
Norton had yet to agree on a film he wanted

00:01:37.929 --> 00:01:43.289
to do, so the company offered him The Italian
Job. After Norton told the studio that he

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:48.469
didn't want to do the film, the studio politely
informed him that he had to do it, or they

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:53.929
would sue. Norton complied, taking the role,
but he refused to do any promotional work

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:59.039
for the film, obviously a bit angry about
the situation. And you wouldn’t like him

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:02.179
when he’s angry.

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:04.340
Natalie Portman

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.970
By the time Natalie Portman agreed to appear
in Thor, Marvel Studios already had big plans.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:14.280
They were signing just about every actor who
appeared in their movies to multiple-movie

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.380
contracts. They had even signed Samuel L.
Jackson to a multi-picture deal, and his first

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:24.690
appearance as Nick Fury was only a cameo after
the credits of Iron Man. Portman must have

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.940
missed this part of her contract, as she later
wanted nothing to do with the Thor sequel

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:33.350
when it came time time to film it. Of course,
we can't blame Portman for not wanting to

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:39.390
appear in Thor: The Dark World. When development
began in April of 2011, Portman was still

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.750
pregnant, and she had made it known that she
wanted to take time off from film work to

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:49.490
care for her child. In addition to that, Marvel
fired Patty Jenkins, whom Portman had recommended

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:53.860
to direct the movie, so that didn't sit well
with the actress either. While there's ample

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.700
evidence to suggest that Portman didn’t
want to do the film, she has since denied

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.440
that she was forced to appear in it.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.400
Emily Blunt

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.870
After appearing in Fox Studios’ The Devil
Wears Prada, many studios sought out Emily

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:14.040
Blunt for their films. Even Marvel Studios
wanted her to appear in Iron Man 2. However,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.510
Fox Studios preferred that she stay with them
and appear in their remake of Gulliver's Travels

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:24.440
instead, starring Jack Black. Luckily for
Fox, and unluckily for Blunt, her Prada contract

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:29.690
had a clause that required her to star in
another Fox-made movie. And they used it on

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:35.090
a movie that wound up becoming a critical
and financial bomb. Fortunately, Blunt's career

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:39.430
wasn't damaged too much by this movie, as
she has gone on to make many successful films

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.250
since then.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.020
Keanu Reeves

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.980
The Watcher is proof that not all of our friends
have our best interests at heart, as Keanu

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:52.640
Reeves learned. In this case, the so-called
friend was Joe Charbanic, the director of

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:58.100
The Watcher, who had also filmed Reeves' band
Dogstar while on tour. Shortly after Reeves'

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:03.230
huge success with The Matrix, Charbanic allegedly
forged Reeves' signature on a contract to

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:08.560
appear in his serial-killer flick. Rather
than deal with a long and costly legal dispute,

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.960
and unable to prove the forgery, Reeves appeared
in the The Watcher. Once the movie was released,

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:18.139
Reeves did nothing to promote it, but for
12 months, he was contractually prevented

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:22.730
from talking about how he got involved in
it. However, once that contract was up, he

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:27.960
didn't hold anything back, saying, "I never
found the script interesting,” and revealing

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.030
his damaged relationship with the director.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.670
Whoopi Goldberg

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:38.490
After her success with Sister Act 2: Back
in the Habit, Whoopi Goldberg was riding high

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:43.750
when producers approached her to star in their
movie Theodore Rex. At the time, Goldberg

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.950
orally agreed to appear in the movie, but
over the next two years, something happened

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:53.800
to change Goldberg's mind. Our guess? It was
probably the animatronic, talking dinosaur:

00:04:53.800 --> 00:05:00.280
(weird dinosaur sounds)

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.690
She attempted to back out of it, but a previous
court case involving Kim Basinger backing

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:09.530
out of Boxing Helena created a precedent that
would have made it very expensive for Goldberg

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:14.970
to duck out. The actress relented and appeared
in the movie. The movie did so horribly on

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:19.639
its test run that it was released direct-to-video,
and has the distinction of being the only

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:26.070
direct-to-video movie to earn a Razzie nomination.
For obvious reasons:

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:32.310
(weird dinosaur singing)

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:32.940
Val Kilmer

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:40.020
Surprisingly, Val Kilmer wanted nothing to
do with Top Gun, the movie that arguably shot

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.990
him to stardom. It was all the result of a
three-picture deal he signed with Paramount.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:50.370
He had completed the first two films of the
deal, Top Secret! and Real Genius, and owed

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:55.560
them one more. In order to get his agent off
his back, Kilmer went to meet with the film's

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.410
director, the late Tony Scott. According to
Kilmer, he went and had the meeting and then

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.639
attempted to leave, but wasn’t immediately
allowed to:

00:06:03.639 --> 00:06:11.300
"Tony ran after me, literally ran after me.
He got in front of the elevator doors and

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.220
said, 'You've gotta do it man!'"

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.919
Scott knew he didn't want to make the movie,
but Kilmer took the role anyway. We bet Kilmer's

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:24.870
glad he took that role now. Kilmer worked
with Scott again in True Romance.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.650
The Entire Cast of Movie 43

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:33.260
Considered one of the worst movies ever made,
Movie 43 has a stellar cast that includes

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:41.040
Bad Catwoman, 300 Abs Guy, House Bunny, Wolverine,
Jackass, McLovin’, Stifler, and Titanic

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:46.360
Lady. How the producer Charles Wessler got
all of these A-List stars to agree to such

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:51.960
an awful movie is a bit of a scandal. Wessler,
responsible for lowbrow films like Shallow

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.480
Hal and There's Something About Mary, somehow
managed to sign Jackman and Winslet and film

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:02.919
their scene sometime in 2009. Wessler then
used their involvement to sign the rest of

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:07.350
the cast. But when the other actors learned
what they were involved in, they tried to

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:13.180
get out. Some, like Colin Farrell, and the
creators of South Park, Trey Parker and Matt

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:17.630
Stone, did manage to get out of their contracts.
And it's been reported that George Clooney

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:22.320
was able to get out of his contract as well,
apparently by telling the producers to, and

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.650
we quote, "F*** off." The rest of the cast
was not so fortunate and were stuck on the

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:32.419
film… allegedly, working at scale rates.
Is there any crueler fate?

00:07:32.419 --> 00:07:35.040
Maybe just having to actually watch Movie
43.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.260
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:43.800
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which star you think got the worst

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:44.300
deal...

